    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d372">

                <pb facs="0532" n="408" sameAs="frus:frus1921v01/pg408"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.74/56: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Crane</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Acting Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-01-08T22:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 8,
                                1921—10 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received January 8—3:25
                        p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>14. Legation’s 467, December 28, 4 p.m. Contract<anchor n="3" xml:id="d372-f1"/>
                    signed today in the presence of Legation representatives, text by the next
                    pouch. Supplementary letter provides that contract becomes effective upon
                    ratification by the company. As the contract provides for overseas
                    communications, Legation considers it to be removed from the scope of the
                    consortium. Attempting maintain secrecy pending ratification.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Crane</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d372-f1" n="3" xml:id="d372-f1-content">
                <p>For text of the contract, see <hi rendition="#italic">List of Contracts of
                        American Nationals with the Chinese Government</hi>, etc., annex VIII
                    (Government Printing Office, 1925).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
